ter 6"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Regulatory pathways"},{"text":"Technical writing"},{"text":"Regulatory submissions"},{"text":"Product registration"},{"text":"Clinical-trial documentation"},{"text":"Manufacturing compliance"},{"text":"Risk management"},{"text":"Quality systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 7"},{"type":"p","text":"Advanced professional focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Regulatory strategy"},{"text":"Submission lifecycle"},{"text":"Regulatory intelligence"},{"text":"Labeling concepts"},{"text":"Change control"},{"text":"Post-market requirements"},{"text":"Audit readiness"},{"text":"Industry internship"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 8"},{"type":"p","text":"Complete:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Regulatory affairs capstone"},{"text":"Industry internship"},{"text":"Mock regulatory submission"},{"text":"Technical documentation portfolio"},{"text":"Final-year project"}]}]},{"heading":"Understand the Product Lifecycle","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Regulatory Affairs professional should understand the complete lifecycle:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Discovery","Development","Preclinical","Clinical","Manufacturing","Regulatory Submission","Approval/Authorization","Commercialization","Post-Market Surveillance"]},{"type":"p","text":"Different products follow different regulatory pathways."},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the fundamentals of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pharmaceuticals"},{"text":"Biologics"},{"text":"Vaccines"},{"text":"Biosimilars"},{"text":"Medical devices"},{"text":"Diagnostics"},{"text":"Biotechnology products"},{"text":"Cell and gene therapies"},{"text":"Laboratory products"}]}]},{"heading":"Regulatory Affairs Fundamentals","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Regulatory strategy"},{"text":"Regulatory pathways"},{"text":"Product classification"},{"text":"Submission requirements"},{"text":"Regulatory documentation"},{"text":"Agency correspondence"},{"text":"Compliance monitoring"},{"text":"Regulatory intelligence"},{"text":"Lifecycle management"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the difference between:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Scientific evidence","Technical documentation","Regulatory submission","Regulatory decision"]}]},{"heading":"Major Regulatory Documents","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop the ability to read and prepare structured documentation."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the fundamentals of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Product dossiers"},{"text":"Technical reports"},{"text":"Clinical documentation"},{"text":"Manufacturing information"},{"text":"Quality documentation"},{"text":"Risk assessments"},{"text":"Stability data"},{"text":"Validation documentation"},{"text":"Regulatory correspondence"},{"text":"Change-control documentation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For pharmaceutical/biological products, become familiar with the general structure and purpose of the Common Technical Document (CTD)."}]},{"heading":"Quality & Manufacturing Knowledge","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Regulatory Affairs Associate should understand how products are manufactured and controlled."},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"h","text":"GMP"},{"type":"p","text":"Good Manufacturing Practice concepts such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Batch records"},{"text":"Deviations"},{"text":"CAPA"},{"text":"Change control"},{"text":"Validation"},{"text":"Qualification"},{"text":"Quality control"},{"text":"Quality assurance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"GLP"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Laboratory documentation"},{"text":"Study integrity"},{"text":"Data recording"},{"text":"Quality systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"GCP"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand fundamentals of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Clinical research"},{"text":"Participant protection"},{"text":"Clinical documentation"},{"text":"Data integrity"},{"text":"Trial oversight"}]}]},{"heading":"Regulatory Frameworks","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop awareness of major regulatory organizations and frameworks."},{"type":"h","text":"India"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the roles of relevant Indian authorities and frameworks, including:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CDSCO"},{"text":"DCGI"},{"text":"Ministry of Health & Family Welfare"},{"text":"ICMR"},{"text":"Department of Biotechnology"},{"text":"State regulatory authorities where applicable"}]},{"type":"h","text":"International"},{"type":"p","text":"Become familiar with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"US FDA"},{"text":"EMA"},{"text":"MHRA"},{"text":"Health Canada"},{"text":"TGA"},{"text":"WHO"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The exact authority and requirements depend on the product type, jurisdiction, and stage of development."}]},{"heading":"ICH Guidelines","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"ICH knowledge is highly valuable for pharmaceutical and biotechnology regulatory careers."},{"type":"p","text":"Develop familiarity with the major guideline families:"},{"type":"h","text":"Quality"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Q1 — Stability"},{"text":"Q2 — Analytical validation"},{"text":"Q3 — Impurities"},{"text":"Q5 — Quality of biotechnological products"},{"text":"Q6 — Specifications"},{"text":"Q7 — GMP for active pharmaceutical ingredients"},{"text":"Q8 — Pharmaceutical development"},{"text":"Q9 — Quality risk management"},{"text":"Q10 — Pharmaceutical quality system"},{"text":"Q11 — Drug-substance development"},{"text":"Q12 — Product lifecycle management"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Safety"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the purpose of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Carcinogenicity studies"},{"text":"Genotoxicity"},{"text":"Toxicology"},{"text":"Reproductive toxicity"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Efficacy"},{"type":"p","text":"Become familiar with concepts around:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Clinical trials"},{"text":"